# CFF citation metadata for SIREN (v2 revision draft; supersedes the v1.0 release metadata).
# NOTE (TODO before any Zenodo deposit): add ORCIDs if desired, and fill in `doi` after the authors tag a release.
# Validate with `cffconvert --validate` or https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or analysis, please cite both this software release
  and the accompanying preprint.
title: >-
  SIREN — leave-one-chromosome-out reassessment of CRISPRi enhancer–gene
  baselines and a corrected Enformer silencing analysis (code, audit and
  machine-checked results)
authors:
  - given-names: Gabriele
    family-names: Bambini
    affiliation: "Università Commerciale Luigi Bocconi, Milano, Italia"
  - given-names: Lorenzo
    family-names: De Santis
    affiliation: "Università Commerciale Luigi Bocconi, Milano, Italia"
  - given-names: Andrea
    family-names: Tangherloni
    affiliation: "Università Commerciale Luigi Bocconi, Milano, Italia"
version: 2.0-draft
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gabriele-Bambini/siren-crispr-reference"
abstract: >-
  Re-analysis of the public EPCrisprBenchmark K562 table (10,356 tested
  element-gene pairs) with leave-one-chromosome-out evaluation and
  cluster-aware bootstrap intervals: unfitted log-distance as the baseline to
  beat, locus-disjoint transfer across screens and cell types, a corrected
  Enformer in-silico-silencing analysis, conformal calibration and selection,
  and an audit of an earlier internal release. Analyses were pre-specified in a
  git-timestamped plan; every number in the manuscript is regenerated by the
  pipeline and checked by script.
keywords:
  - CRISPRi
  - enhancer-gene prediction
  - benchmark
  - Enformer
  - conformal prediction
  - reproducibility
  - functional genomics
